<h1 id="pgtestcom-title" style="color:#0d47a1;font-size:1.5em;font-weight:700;border-bottom:2px solid #90caf9;padding-bottom:0.25em;margin-top:0"><code>pgtestcom</code> — pgbattest run + scoreboard + compare</h1>

**Type:** keyword campaign · **Not always-on** — mention **`pgtestcom`** or `@` this rule.  
**Owns:** (1) one live `pgbattest` campaign for the requested scopes, (2) append/update [`docs/pglpl/PGBATTEST_CATALOG_SCOREBOARD.md`](../../../docs/pglpl/PGBATTEST_CATALOG_SCOREBOARD.md) with the new tip **including wall duration**, (3) detailed **tabular compare** of relevant scopes vs prior run id(s) **in that scoreboard**, (4) a **freshman-plain** summary table in the chat reply.  
**Does not own:** `pgjudge` fix→retry budgets (`pgbattest` / `aciub`); paragraph play-by-play (`pgpbp`); git commit/push (`gitacp`).

## Document outline

1. [When this applies](#when) — trigger + parse defaults.
2. [Locks / defaults](#locks) — ambiguities frozen here.
