<h2 id="scoreboard" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">4. Scoreboard write shape</h2>

Edit [`docs/pglpl/PGBATTEST_CATALOG_SCOREBOARD.md`](../../../docs/pglpl/PGBATTEST_CATALOG_SCOREBOARD.md) following existing **`mrkd`** / §6.xx patterns:

1. **§2 Campaign timeline** — append one row: **run stamp** `YYMMDD-hhmm` (local start) · when/end window if known · what (scopes + model if known) · headline counts · **wall duration** (`Ns` + `~N min`) · log filename · summary stamp if expgtest.
2. **New detail section** — next free `§6.xx` (under the active campaign heading, e.g. Campaign D). Include:
   - Branch / model / allowlist notes if relevant
   - Log + Door C JSON paths
   - **Run stamp** `YYMMDD-hhmm` (local) + summary artifact stamp when present
   - **Wall time** (required)
   - Catalog or subset score (verified / quality_failed / failed_first5 / failed_all)
   - Outcome lists or compact table for **requested** scopes
3. **Compare subsection** inside that §6.xx — the detailed vs-prior table(s) ([§5](#compare)).
4. **§3 Latest known** — update rows for every scope in **this** run (outcome + evidence `§6.xx`). Leave other scopes’ “latest” untouched unless this run was full-23 (then refresh the whole §3 tip sentence).

Do **not** delete prior §6 history.

---

<h2 id="compare" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">5. Compare table shape</h2>

**Scope of compare:** only scopes in `<list_of_scopes>` (or all 23). For each baseline in `<list_of_runs>`, pull that scope’s outcome from that §6 section (or §3 if the detail is thin — prefer the named §6).

**Required HTML table** (`mrkd` colors):

| Column | Content |
|--------|---------|
| Scope | catalog id |
| Each prior `§6.xx` | outcome (`verified` / `quality_failed` / `failed_first5` / `failed_all` / n/a) |
| This run (`§6.new`) | outcome |
| Delta vs each prior | `improved` / `held` / `regressed` / `n/a` |

Also record **headline deltas** when useful: verified count, Door A/B/C fail counts, wall time vs prior (if prior wall known).

**Mechanics (optional but preferred):** 2–6 bullets under the table for scopes that changed — name the likely contract (verify / Injection Gate / punch / Door C), not a full `pgpbp`.

Delta labels stay freshman-readable: **improved** = worse→better door outcome; **regressed** = better→worse; **held** = same class.

---

<h2 id="reply" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">6. Chat reply shape (mandatory)</h2>

After scoreboard edits, reply for a **college freshman**:

1. One–two sentence tip (new `§6.xx`, wall time, verified / fail mix).
2. **Layman summary table** (mandatory), e.g.:

| Scope (or group) | Before (prior tip) | Now | Plain English |
|------------------|--------------------|-----|---------------|
| … | verified / Door A fail / … | … | got better / worse / same |

3. At most **3** bullets: biggest wins, biggest regressions, next watchlist.  
No jargon dump; define one label if needed (`verified` = A+B+C ok).

